The Guild of Prophets          NannyMUD Times                         Page 3
by Anji

  The dreaded prophets of Nanny is once again back, the reopening
  of the future-tellers of old are here once again. Aspiring for
  the real goal of life, Armageddon!

  The adventure of being a prophet starts off in Profezzorns
  area. One must search through the forest towards the monolith
  and there climb the rocks to find the guild hall.
  The begining of the aspiring prophet starts with simple
  predictions about the depressing future, but once one get
  started the mysteries of percepting the clouded future gets
  easy to see. As the knowledge seeps into the mind, the traces
  that binds everything get's clear.

  The life of a prophet is a lone life, they prefer to be by
  themselves. But because of this prophets are not solitaire,
  the prophet often goes around and telling other players about
  the hidden future and of course donating money to the poor.
  What would a life without charity be?

  The guild is pretty easy to get started in, and to advance is
  a simple use your powers - gain more guild points. You can also
  get guild points by becoming older and more wise. Isn't that
  what we all aspire to be?

  A prophet is not a mighty warrior and dont rely on tough armour
  and heavy weapons for damaging their foes. The way of a prophet
  is more about knowledge than about strengh and bashing abilities.
  Because of that, the player tends to know more about the world
  than about how to best finish of a kill.

  The guild masters of the Prophets are: Profezzorn and Vulcan.

